al phosphorus and no bone pain provide weak support for primary hyperparathyroidism, but elevated alkaline phosphatase shifts probability toward malignancy."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute constitutional presentation (weight loss, cognitive slowing) with normal serum phosphorus and elevated alkaline phosphatase argue against antacid-induced hypercalcemia and favor mal…", "summary": "The constitutional symptoms and elevated alkaline phosphatase moderately support malignancy while reducing plausibility of antacid overuse."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the absence of muscle aches and normal phosphorus inconsistent with vitamin D toxicity and more supportive of malignancy?", "summary": "Classic vitamin D toxicity features (muscle aches) are absent, which weakens its likelihood and slightly increases malignancy probability."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the elevated alkaline phosphatase (150 U/L) inconsistent with primary hyperparathyroidism and more supportive of malignancy-related hypercalcemia?", "summary": "Elevated alkaline phosphatase strongly supports malignancy-related hypercalcemia and weakly argues against primary hyperparathyroidism."}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch (B1.1) has posterior < 0.75. Dangerous alternative B2.1 (primary hyperparathyroidism) remains with posterior 0.056 and danger 0.8. B3 (malignancy) has low posterior but high danger (0.9) and requires exclusion. Insufficient certainty to terminate."}, "turn_budget_used": 2, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.55, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.22497343702969763, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely explanation of this patient's current presentation?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Antacid overuse"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Increased 1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Increased parathyroid hormone"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Malignancy"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Viral illness"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Hyperparathyroidism', 'Hypervalinemia', 'Elevated alkaline phosphatase'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.599}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B1.1", "label": "Milk-Alkali Syndrome (Antacid Overuse)", "posterior": 0.225, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 1, "disconfirming": 2, "last_disconfirming_digest": "The constitutional symptoms and elevated alkaline phosphatase moderately support malignancy while reducing plausibility…"}, "action_intents": [{"t": 2, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B1.2", "B4", "B2.1"]}}
